                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  img
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="7").
                  <img />
        h2#block-expansion
          | Block Expansion
          a.header-anchor(href="#block-expansion", aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p To save space, Pug provides an inline syntax for nested tags.
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="2")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="365980985")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  a: img
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="7").
                  <a><img /></a>
        h2#self-closing-tags
          | Self-Closing Tags
          a.header-anchor(href="#self-closing-tags", aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p
          | Tags such as
          code img
          | ,
          code meta
          | , and
          code link
          | are automatically self-closing (unless you use the XML doctype).
        p
          | You can also explicitly self close a tag by appending the
          code /
          | character. Only do this if you know what you’re doing.
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="3")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="-577472172")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  foo/
                  foo(bar='baz')/
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="7").
                  <foo />
                  <foo bar="baz" />
        h2#rendered-whitespace
          | Rendered Whitespace
          a.header-anchor(href="#rendered-whitespace", aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p
          | Whitespace is removed from the beginning and end of tags, so that you have control over whether the rendered HTML elements touch or not. Whitespace control is generally handled via
          a(href="plain-text.html#whitespace-control") plain text
          | .
